    "### Autodiferenciação\n",
    "\n",
    "Para $f(\\mathbf{x})=\\sum_i x_i^2$, temos $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}}f=2\\mathbf{x}$. O PyTorch registra o grafo das operações quando `requires_grad=True` e calcula o gradiente com `backward()`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 60,
   "id": "XWk5OUst3QJA",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "XWk5OUst3QJA"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "f(x) = 14.0\n",
      "gradiente calculado: tensor([ 2., -4.,  6.])\n",
      "gradiente esperado: tensor([ 2., -4.,  6.])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "x = torch.tensor([1.0, -2.0, 3.0], requires_grad=True)\n",
    "f = (x ** 2).sum()\n",
    "f.backward()\n",
    "print(\"f(x) =\", f.item())\n",
    "print(\"gradiente calculado:\", x.grad)\n",
    "print(\"gradiente esperado:\", 2 * x.detach())\n"
   ]
  },
